\par }{If you\rquote re like me you have many CD-R disks that you\rquote 
ve recorded. Trying to find a file on these disks can be very frustrating. This is why I created CDScan. CDScan is a utility that will create a catalog of your CD disks. This will make using and finding files on these disks very easy. By catalo
ging the contents of the disks you can easily find the single file that you are looking for without having to search each disk separately, if you ever done this you know exactly what I\rquote m talking about.
\par 
\par Using CDScan is very simple, scan the CD create a unique Label for the Volume and write it to a file. After your done mark the CD Case with the Volume Label and your done. 
\par 
\par Example:
\par I have 5 CD\rquote s that I have recorded, I created a Catalog containing all 5 CD\rquote s conte
nts. When I was done I created a CD jewel case insert for each CD with the CDScan Volume label printed on the spline. Volume1, Volume2, Volume 3, Volume 4, Volume 5, etc. (I prefer using the word Volume to mark my disks, you can use anything that you
\rquote d like Disk 1, Disk 2, etc.) Now finding files is a breeze! I search for the file I\rquote 
m looking for using the CDScan search function and it informs me if it found it and what Volume its on, all I have to do is grab the CD Volume and get my file!
\par 
\par Comments or suggestions on CDScan can be sent to mmonti@mminternet.com
